WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:03.369
 Trevor, Victor,
congratulations.

00:00:03.470 --> 00:00:05.371
You guys have made it to
the third and final round

00:00:05.437 --> 00:00:07.807
of this competition, and now
we're sending you to your home

00:00:07.874 --> 00:00:12.378
forges for four grueling days
to recreate this iconic weapon

00:00:12.445 --> 00:00:13.246
from history.

00:00:15.815 --> 00:00:17.250
The épée-de-combat.

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:20.986
Gentlemen, this blade can be
seen wielded by Arya Stark

00:00:21.053 --> 00:00:22.588
from Game of Thrones.

00:00:22.655 --> 00:00:24.357
[laughs]

00:00:24.457 --> 00:00:26.526
Good luck, bladesmiths,
we'll see you in four days.

00:00:30.896 --> 00:00:33.065 line:8%
 It's day one, and
I'm about to start

00:00:33.132 --> 00:00:35.869
making the épee-de-combat.

00:00:35.935 --> 00:00:37.970
I've come to call it
the holy [bleep] sword,

00:00:38.037 --> 00:00:41.441
because it is so
thin and so long,

00:00:41.507 --> 00:00:45.378
it's going to be a very,
very difficult blade to make.

00:00:45.478 --> 00:00:47.280
I've chosen 5160.

00:00:47.346 --> 00:00:50.283
It's good, tough, spring steel.

00:00:50.349 --> 00:00:52.619
I want to make this
blade as rigid as I can,

00:00:52.719 --> 00:00:53.886
but still flexible.

00:00:53.952 --> 00:00:55.221
Yeah, the wheels are turning.

00:00:55.287 --> 00:00:57.557
They're pretty rusty,
but they're turning.

00:00:57.624 --> 00:00:59.525
It is the end of day one.

00:00:59.625 --> 00:01:02.295
I hit the link I was
aiming for to a point

00:01:02.361 --> 00:01:04.330
where I say it's in good shape.

00:01:04.396 --> 00:01:07.767 line:8%
I'm hoping to be
grinding blade tomorrow.

00:01:07.834 --> 00:01:09.669 line:8%
 We're here in
San Antonio, Texas.

00:01:09.769 --> 00:01:11.036
Let's get the fire going.

00:01:11.103 --> 00:01:12.906
I've never made
such a light sword,

00:01:13.006 --> 00:01:15.975
so to make this as light
as it's supposed to be

00:01:16.042 --> 00:01:17.510
is definitely a challenge.

00:01:17.577 --> 00:01:21.080
My plan is to use the 5160
for the actual sword itself,

00:01:21.146 --> 00:01:23.049
and then for the
pommel and the guard,

00:01:23.149 --> 00:01:25.017
I'm gonna see if I can
bring out some Damascus

00:01:25.117 --> 00:01:27.153
to throw my twist on it.

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:30.590
It's too wide, so I'm
turning it down quite a bit,

00:01:30.656 --> 00:01:33.392
little at a time.

00:01:33.493 --> 00:01:36.196
Now that I've got my sword
to a comfortable state,

00:01:36.262 --> 00:01:39.365
I start cutting some pieces for
billets, three small stacks,

00:01:39.432 --> 00:01:41.734
so I can make my
pommel, quillon,

00:01:41.801 --> 00:01:44.337
and guard out of Damascus.

00:01:44.403 --> 00:01:46.672
 This is the start of day two.

00:01:46.739 --> 00:01:48.041
Rolling along pretty good.

00:01:48.141 --> 00:01:50.876
Today I'm going to start
trying to put the crease

00:01:50.976 --> 00:01:54.747
in the back for the fullers.

00:01:54.848 --> 00:01:56.482
I've never ground
fullers before.

00:01:56.549 --> 00:01:58.818 line:8%
It's a huge learning
curve for me,

00:01:58.884 --> 00:02:01.420 line:14%
so it's going to be critical.

00:02:01.521 --> 00:02:03.489
I get the fuller
cut into the back,

00:02:03.589 --> 00:02:08.928
I'm trying to grind on the front
side, and they're not working.

00:02:09.028 --> 00:02:11.230
It's not cutting to the
depth that I wanted.

00:02:11.297 --> 00:02:12.932
It's grinding it flat.

00:02:13.032 --> 00:02:16.569
It's frustrating
the hell out of me.

00:02:16.636 --> 00:02:19.805
[bleep] I've messed
up my center line.

00:02:19.905 --> 00:02:20.940
Badly.

00:02:21.007 --> 00:02:22.875
I've got like 6
center lines now.

00:02:22.975 --> 00:02:26.112
I wanted to have both sides of
the fullers completed today,

00:02:26.178 --> 00:02:28.447
and I still got to get
this blade quenched,

00:02:28.514 --> 00:02:31.550 line:8%
so I hope that I can
finish this blade.

00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:35.421 line:8%
 It's day two, I'm trying to
get the Damascus forge-wielded,

00:02:35.522 --> 00:02:36.823
sorted to shape.

00:02:36.890 --> 00:02:38.324
This is going to
be my guard, those

00:02:38.424 --> 00:02:39.659
are going to be my quillons.

00:02:39.759 --> 00:02:41.761
So right now I'm just
thinning it down so they

00:02:41.861 --> 00:02:43.228
don't have so much weight.

00:02:43.295 --> 00:02:45.498
I have the pommel
billets, and I started

00:02:45.564 --> 00:02:48.567
drawing out the quillons,
I think I'm happy with it.

00:02:48.667 --> 00:02:51.771
Now that I finish up the handle
pieces, it's time to quench.

00:02:51.838 --> 00:02:55.741
You can see my blade shaking,
I'm shaking so much right now.

00:02:55.808 --> 00:02:57.377
This is all do or die.

00:03:03.783 --> 00:03:06.351
Nice and straight that way,
nice and straight that way.

00:03:06.452 --> 00:03:08.120 line:8%
I left it just a
little bit thick,

00:03:08.187 --> 00:03:09.355
so I can do all
my hollow grinds,

00:03:09.421 --> 00:03:11.824
and then all I have left
would be the fit up,

00:03:11.890 --> 00:03:13.492 line:14%
and put a handle.

00:03:13.592 --> 00:03:16.696 line:8%
 On day three, I need
to finish grinding

00:03:16.763 --> 00:03:18.397
my fullers on both sides.

00:03:18.464 --> 00:03:21.267
I need heat treatment, I need
to shape it into the blade

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:22.668
that it's going to be.

00:03:22.768 --> 00:03:25.538
Yesterday, I failed miserably
at grinding fullers,

00:03:25.638 --> 00:03:30.676
so today has to go
better, or I'm in trouble.

00:03:30.743 --> 00:03:34.113
I worked my fullers down to
a point where I'm satisfied,

00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:36.216
and I decided that
it's time to quench.

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:42.622
She took, I think
that's pretty good.

00:03:42.688 --> 00:03:45.825
The épée-de-combat is
supposed to be light and fast.

00:03:45.892 --> 00:03:49.828
And my blade turned out to be
really thin and pretty light.

00:03:49.928 --> 00:03:53.266 line:14%
I think it'll be a good blade.

00:03:53.333 --> 00:03:54.533 line:14%
 Final stretch.

00:03:54.633 --> 00:03:56.302 line:8%
Still a lot to do,
and majority of day's

00:03:56.402 --> 00:03:57.803
gonna be on the handle.

00:03:57.904 --> 00:04:01.007
I'm going to go with some
stabilized Buckeye burl.

00:04:01.107 --> 00:04:02.508
I have two different
tones, and it'll

00:04:02.608 --> 00:04:04.477
give it a good two tone look.

00:04:07.813 --> 00:04:09.415
I like it so far.

00:04:09.515 --> 00:04:11.150
It's still a little
heavy, but it's

00:04:11.250 --> 00:04:13.051
pieced together pretty good.

00:04:13.152 --> 00:04:14.887
I'm finishing!

00:04:14.954 --> 00:04:16.221
Thank God!

00:04:16.288 --> 00:04:17.723
 All right, bladesmiths.

00:04:17.823 --> 00:04:20.026
This is the kill test.

00:04:20.092 --> 00:04:23.295
I will take your weapon and
deliver some thrust and slashes

00:04:23.395 --> 00:04:26.231
on our dummy from the North.

00:04:26.298 --> 00:04:27.233
Trevor, you're up first.

00:04:27.333 --> 00:04:27.967
You ready for this?

00:04:28.067 --> 00:04:28.935
 I'm ready.

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:02.067
 All right, Trevor.

00:05:02.134 --> 00:05:03.069
First up.

00:05:03.136 --> 00:05:04.370
It is so light.

00:05:04.437 --> 00:05:06.039
Just like a needle.

00:05:06.105 --> 00:05:08.140
Your point here
allows for a very deep

00:05:08.206 --> 00:05:10.209
penetration without any effort.

00:05:10.309 --> 00:05:12.745
Overall, sir, it will kill.

00:05:12.812 --> 00:05:13.913
Good job.

00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:15.047
All right, Victor.
Your turn.

00:05:15.113 --> 00:05:15.982
Are you ready?
- Ready.

00:05:50.550 --> 00:05:51.483
 All right, Victor.

00:05:51.550 --> 00:05:53.152
Let's talk about
your sword here.

00:05:53.219 --> 00:05:54.954
It's not very light.

00:05:55.054 --> 00:05:58.624
Overall, though, it's
pointy enough to thrust,

00:05:58.691 --> 00:06:03.629
the edge with the weight
cuts, and it'll kill.

00:06:03.696 --> 00:06:04.329
 Thank you.

00:06:04.396 --> 00:06:05.398
 All right, gentlemen.

00:06:05.464 --> 00:06:07.733
It's time for the strength test.

00:06:07.799 --> 00:06:11.104
To test the strength and overall
construction of your blades,

00:06:11.170 --> 00:06:14.273
just like an ice pick, I'm
going to be chipping ice.

00:06:14.340 --> 00:06:15.207
 Trevor, you're up first.

00:06:15.274 --> 00:06:15.941
You're ready?

00:06:16.041 --> 00:06:16.843
 I'm ready.

00:06:39.131 --> 00:06:40.532
 OK, Trevor.

00:06:40.599 --> 00:06:44.303
You did pick up a
slight bend in your tip.

00:06:44.403 --> 00:06:46.706
Having said that, I
mean, this thing is

00:06:46.772 --> 00:06:48.807
so light, which is fantastic.

00:06:48.874 --> 00:06:50.342
 Thank you.

00:06:50.409 --> 00:06:52.044
 All right, Victor.

00:06:52.145 --> 00:06:53.312
You are up.
Are you ready, sir?

00:06:53.379 --> 00:06:54.180
 Ready.

00:07:13.565 --> 00:07:17.269
 Victor, first off,
blade is same shape

00:07:17.336 --> 00:07:18.337
as when we started out.

00:07:18.403 --> 00:07:20.639
Tip's still there, it's fine.

00:07:20.706 --> 00:07:23.041
Your fullers are there,
but they're not very deep.

00:07:23.141 --> 00:07:27.779
And by not having them very
deep, this blade is very heavy.

00:07:27.846 --> 00:07:31.016
Having said that, it's a strong
blade, it took no damage.

00:07:31.083 --> 00:07:31.750
So well done.

00:07:31.850 --> 00:07:32.451
 Thank you.

00:07:32.551 --> 00:07:33.953
 All right, bladesmiths.

00:07:34.053 --> 00:07:35.254
This is the sharpness test.

00:07:35.321 --> 00:07:38.591
This steel can stab
and waterbag slice.

00:07:38.658 --> 00:07:39.892
I will take your
weapon, I'm going

00:07:39.992 --> 00:07:42.762
to test the tip by
thrusting into the cans,

00:07:42.828 --> 00:07:45.264
and I'm going to slash the bag.

00:07:45.331 --> 00:07:46.365
Trevor, you're up first.
You ready?

00:07:46.465 --> 00:07:47.700
 I'm ready.

00:08:04.684 --> 00:08:05.918
 All right, Trevor.

00:08:05.985 --> 00:08:08.120
No issues at all in
stabbing the can,

00:08:08.220 --> 00:08:11.423
and the cut with your tip on
that bag, you can see it's

00:08:11.490 --> 00:08:13.359
a straight cut all
the way through.

00:08:13.459 --> 00:08:15.861
Overall, sir, it'll cut.

00:08:15.961 --> 00:08:17.063
 Thank you.

00:08:17.163 --> 00:08:18.030
 All right, Victor.

00:08:18.097 --> 00:08:18.730
Your turn.
So you ready?

00:08:18.797 --> 00:08:19.565
 Ready.

00:08:39.185 --> 00:08:40.453
 All right, Victor.

00:08:40.553 --> 00:08:43.022
First up in the stabbing
test, on one of the thrusts,

00:08:43.122 --> 00:08:46.224
it pushed the can in more than
penetrated all the way through,

00:08:46.291 --> 00:08:47.993
but your edge is sharp.

00:08:48.093 --> 00:08:50.362
On the bag, it cut cleanly
all the way through.

00:08:50.428 --> 00:08:52.931
And more importantly, it'll cut.

00:08:52.998 --> 00:08:53.632
 Thank you.

00:08:53.699 --> 00:08:54.833
 All right, gentlemen.

00:08:54.933 --> 00:08:57.836
I finished my discussion
with your judges,

00:08:57.936 --> 00:08:59.505
and they've made
their final decision.

00:08:59.571 --> 00:09:04.810
Our new Forged in Fire
champion is Trevor.

00:09:04.911 --> 00:09:05.944
Congratulations.

00:09:06.011 --> 00:09:07.880
You're the new Forged
in Fire champion.

00:09:07.946 --> 00:09:10.749
Victor, unfortunately your
blade didn't make the cut

00:09:10.816 --> 00:09:12.084
by the narrowest of margins.

00:09:12.151 --> 00:09:14.053
And David Baker's
going to tell you why.

00:09:14.119 --> 00:09:17.122
 Victor, the épéé-de-combat
was supposed to be a lightning

00:09:17.189 --> 00:09:18.724
fast thrusting sword.

00:09:18.824 --> 00:09:21.393
The weight of your
blade led it to be just

00:09:21.459 --> 00:09:23.262
a more difficult weapon to use.

00:09:23.328 --> 00:09:24.863
That's why we're letting you go.

00:09:24.963 --> 00:09:28.266
 Victor, unfortunately,
today your blade

00:09:28.333 --> 00:09:29.602
doesn't make the cut.

00:09:29.668 --> 00:09:30.836
I'd like to invite you
to shake our hands,

00:09:30.902 --> 00:09:32.270
shake your competitor's
hand, and then

00:09:32.337 --> 00:09:34.406
please leave the forge.

00:09:34.472 --> 00:09:35.941
 This was a great experience.

00:09:36.007 --> 00:09:38.310
And just holding my
head high, just to know

00:09:38.410 --> 00:09:41.680
I've had this opportunity to
build this historical weapon.

00:09:41.747 --> 00:09:43.849
Performed well, and
I'm proud of it.

00:09:43.949 --> 00:09:46.819
First thing I do when I go
home, kiss the wife, my son,

00:09:46.919 --> 00:09:51.190
and start forging and get
ready for my next knife show.

00:09:51.290 --> 00:09:53.025
 Trevor, congratulations.

00:09:53.125 --> 00:09:55.327
You are our new Forged
in Fire champion,

00:09:55.394 --> 00:09:59.197
and that's a title that comes
with a check for $10,000.

00:09:59.297 --> 00:10:00.132
Good job, brother.

00:10:00.199 --> 00:10:02.301
Come on forward, my friend.

00:10:02.368 --> 00:10:03.602
 Good job.

00:10:03.669 --> 00:10:07.073
 I can't believe that
I won Forged in Fire.

00:10:07.173 --> 00:10:08.841
Feeling better than good.

00:10:08.907 --> 00:10:11.143
The most fun I've had in years.

00:10:11.210 --> 00:10:14.546
With the $10,000 I have,
I may buy a new sander,

00:10:14.646 --> 00:10:18.684
but most of it will
go to my wife, though.

